How to Grow Strawberries

**Soil**  
Strawberries grow in most soils that work for garden plants. Dig the soil deep, about 18 to 20 inches, and add compost or manure so the soil is rich. If the ground is wet, make sure it dries well.

**When to Plant**  
In the northern states, the best time to plant strawberry plants is in spring, during April and May. Plant them when the plants start growing and before they flower. This is also a good time to plant many strawberries together.

**Planting Pots**  
If you have small plants in pots, you can plant them in August and September when it is hot and dry. The little ball of dirt around the roots keeps them healthy. This way you don’t have to water or shade them as much.

