 Humans can do many things that no other animals, even our closest relatives like chimps and gorillas, can do. We are the only species that has created languages with a set of rules—a grammar—that requires words to be in a specific order. You might have seen monkeys call each other, for example a "koo" call that shows friendliness, but you have never seen one write a letter and think about spelling! We can also guess how a friend feels just by looking at their face or hearing their voice, whether they are happy or sad. Moreover, we pass on the knowledge we have learned about the world and the universe from one generation to the next—that is why we go to school. Teaching children about the world is part of human culture, another unique trait. Language, predicting a friend’s mood, and culture are all examples of what makes humans special.

