Bryant was a thoughtful boy who could write poems better than many adults. Yet, in many ways he was an ordinary child. He was quiet and studied hard in class, but he liked to play outside. He and his classmates liked to build small dams on a nearby stream and float rafts made from old boards. In the winter, they slid on ice and made snow forts, calling them strongholds. They divided into two teams, used snowballs as weapons, and fought for control of the forts. Bryant was fast and good at running, but because he was small, he did not stand out in the battles. During long evenings, Bryant and his older brother Austin pretended to be heroes from the Iliad. They armed themselves with swords, spears, and homemade armor and staged the Trojan War in the barn.

