Electromagnets are magnets made with electricity. You can make them stronger by putting more loops of copper wire around an iron nail, or by turning up the electric current. A man named William Sturgeon first built an electromagnet in 1825.  
The great thing about an electromagnet is that you can turn it on and off with a battery, unlike a regular magnet that always stays on.  
